      "answer": "It depends on your county and the specific area of the system. Florida defines certain surfaces as \"obstructed land\" that can interfere with an onsite sewage system, though turf is not named. North Carolina requires the owner to keep vegetation over the dispersal field and repair area and keep structures and traffic off it. Ask the responsible county office before you plan a layout over any part of a septic system."
