      "question": "Do I need a county grading permit to install artificial turf in unincorporated Jefferson or Arapahoe County?",
      "answer": "In unincorporated Jefferson County, a Grading Permit is required once disturbed area reaches 0.5 acres, and related or connected projects on one site count together toward that line even if permit-free on their own. In unincorporated Arapahoe County, the Land Development Code requires a GESC permit for any land disturbance unless the county's GESC Manual exempts it, and even exempt work still needs erosion controls. Confirm your project with the county before you schedule, at 303-349-2368."
