          "For a homeowner planning a layout in a mapped area, the practical sequence is: confirm your address is mapped, confirm which class applies — the code separates Class 1 and Class 2 site requirements by fire intensity classification (low, moderate, high) set on the local map — and get the 5-foot material call from your building department before ordering material. Beyond 5 feet, Section 503.2, the Intermediate Zone (5-30 feet), moves to a fuel-modification standard aimed at removing dead plant material and fuel accumulations rather than mandating hard surfaces, which is a different, looser test than the Immediate Zone's noncombustible-materials list."
