      "question": "Can a North Carolina HOA in Brunswick County stop artificial turf or a putting green?",
      "answer": "Chapter 47F, the Planned Community Act, doesn't mention turf. It sets rules for how an association runs itself and how it can fine you, not what your yard has to look like. That answer lives in your community's own declaration and architectural guidelines. Get the declaration, submit a full layout to the architectural committee, and get approval in writing before you sign anything."
